I think (but I'm not sure ;) ) that haven't much to do with NetHack itself
but with a "non-compatiblety" between the program "patch" (or "diff") from
the (imho) mostly used OS to play (and patch ;) ) NetHack: Linux (a
GNU-program I think) and the FreeBSD pendant.
I know that "problem" from make and gmake.

Nevertheless I write here because it is a NetHack-relevant problem and
eventually I forgot something to do _before_ running "patch" what wasn't
written in [2] (where is only an instruction for patching on Windows at the
time).

So my question: Is there somebody who knows what was my mistake? Is somebody
using FreeBSD for playing NetHack and knows how to patch it?

